{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1426438-in-the-future-talents-become-captain-future","id":1426438,"title":"In the Future Talents...Become Captain Future","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-28T02:42:04-08:00","id":1426438,"title":"In the Future Talents...Become Captain Future","content":"I had an amusing realization. In the Trinity core, you get the fact that novas more or less evolve beyond this universe, charting out their individual paths of transcendence. <br /> Psions... well they evolve, but a lot of psions eventually seem to become hive minds or disembodied intelligences. <br /> <br /> Talents don't get that. They get increasing luck and the ability to tell the universe &quot;no, you&quot; beyond even Mercer... but they don't transcend.<br /> <br /> And it struck me--Talents are the space opera guys. They are these incredible, superhumans, who even so, remain <i>human.</i> They're the future fo Edmund Hamilton, Frank Herbert, Robert Heinlein, rather than the more transhuman futures envisioned by later generations of writers. <br /> <br /> MAybe not a big thought, but it gave me a chuckle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T08:20:49-08:00","id":1426466,"title":"","content":"I can see it. They are the humans who are just a bit MORE than us. They are just a bit better in every way. They are the ones we read about in those books and go 'oh cool, look at the adventure they are having'. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I can totally see this. <br /> <br /